From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BPI-SINOVOIP <support@banana-pi.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] k1-x: define ramdisk_addr_r and fdt_addr_r for extlinux boot

The extlinux fallback added for Armbian images runs sysboot, and
pxe_utils needs ramdisk_addr_r and fdt_addr_r whenever a label has
initrd or fdt lines.  The default environment only carried the
vendor names ramdisk_addr and dtb_addr, so the Armbian label was
skipped with "failure retrieving initrd" and an MBR SD card stopped
at the U-Boot prompt.

Point both variables at the existing RAMDISK_LOAD_ADDR and
DTB_LOAD_ADDR so the extlinux path uses the same layout as the
vendor boot flow.

Signed-off-by: BPI-SINOVOIP <support@banana-pi.org>
---
 include/configs/k1-x.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/configs/k1-x.h b/include/configs/k1-x.h
index 3e83e03..1660667 100644
--- a/include/configs/k1-x.h
+++ b/include/configs/k1-x.h
@@ -194,6 +194,8 @@ struct boot_storage_op
 	"kernel_addr_r=" __stringify(CONFIG_FASTBOOT_BUF_ADDR) "\0" \
 	"ramdisk_addr=" __stringify(RAMDISK_LOAD_ADDR) "\0" \
 	"dtb_addr=" __stringify(DTB_LOAD_ADDR) "\0" \
+	"ramdisk_addr_r=" __stringify(RAMDISK_LOAD_ADDR) "\0" \
+	"fdt_addr_r=" __stringify(DTB_LOAD_ADDR) "\0" \
 	"scriptaddr=0x2c100000\0" \
 	"pxefile_addr_r=0x0c200000\0" \
 	"splashimage=" __stringify(CONFIG_FASTBOOT_BUF_ADDR) "\0" \
